**7. Sensitive Equality — `toStringFormat()`** (line 85)

```java
assertEquals("Catalog(items=1)", catalog.toString());
```

This assertion is coupled to the exact `toString()` format string. Any cosmetic change (e.g., adding a space, renaming the label) breaks the test without any behavior change.

**Refactor:** Assert the semantic property instead, or if the format is contractual, extract the expected format:

```java
@Test
void toStringContainsItemCount() {
    catalog.add("a", 1);
    assertAll(
        () -> assertTrue(catalog.toString().contains("1")),
        () -> assertTrue(catalog.toString().startsWith("Catalog"))
    );
}
```

