**8. Exception Handling in Tests — `addNullSkuManualCatch()`** (line 92)

```java
try {
    catalog.add(null, 1);
    fail("should have thrown");
} catch (Exception ex) {
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

Manual `try/catch` + `fail()` is the pre-JUnit 5 idiom. It catches the broad `Exception` rather than `IllegalArgumentException`, and only checks the message is non-null — a very weak assertion. If the wrong exception type is thrown, the test still passes.

**Refactor:** Use `assertThrows` (already demonstrated in `addThrowsOnNegativeCount`):

```java
@Test
void addRejectsNullSku() {
    IllegalArgumentException ex = assertThrows(
        IllegalArgumentException.class,
        () -> catalog.add(null, 1));
    assertTrue(ex.getMessage().contains("sku is required"));
}
```

